{"hash":"8a67b48d02c2bcfd","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":75.237,"said":"You are in the sabhamandapa, the hall before the sanctum, among its carved stone pillars. This hall is the newest thing here. In January 2026 the temple closed its doors for five months while the old hall gave way to a new, larger one, built for the crowds who come today, and darshan began again that June. The sanctum beyond has not changed. Notice something: from here you cannot see the Jyotirlinga. As in many Shiva temples, the sanctum lies below the level of the hall, and you must go down five steps to reach it. At its doorway, the trust tells us, Ganesha waits on the left, and on the right Kalabhairava, the guardian. Every day the temple opens at five in the morning with puja, and at half past seven in the evening the worship is performed again. On the great nights, Mahashivratri and Tripurari Purnima, there is a maha-aarti, and later the Lord’s palanquin goes out in procession. Now, step by step, come down with me. Bhimashankar is waiting below.\n\nDid you know? The trust asks pilgrims to keep silence inside the temple and simply chant ‘Om Namah Shivaya’.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":964},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":980,"end":1074}],"words":[[0.098,0.192,0,3],[0.302,0.18,4,7],[0.495,0.096,8,10],[0.603,0.084,11,14],[0.699,0.793,15,27],[1.721,0.108,29,32],[1.841,0.276,33,37],[2.129,0.3,38,44],[2.442,0.084,45,48],[2.538,0.649,49,56],[3.463,0.325,58,63],[3.8,0.168,64,67],[3.98,0.361,68,74],[4.353,0.385,75,80],[4.75,0.505,81,88],[6.154,0.288,90,94],[6.454,0.397,95,99],[6.863,0.12,100,102],[6.995,0.072,103,106],[7.079,0.481,107,113],[7.572,0.228,114,119],[7.812,0.349,120,124],[9.038,0.144,126,128],[9.195,1.899,129,141],[11.106,0.108,142,145],[11.226,0.397,146,152],[11.635,0.397,153,159],[12.043,0.156,160,163],[12.212,0.337,164,169],[12.56,0.132,170,173],[12.704,0.349,174,178],[13.065,0.409,179,185],[13.486,0.228,186,191],[13.726,0.072,192,195],[13.81,0.24